; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Inside and Outside Angles
; CATEGORY: Shapes & Polygons
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     angles, polygon, arc, exterior angle, table
; SUMMARY:  Marks the turtle's turn and the inside angle at every corner of six polygons and prints a table of them.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Six regular polygons, from 3 to 8 sides. At every corner a red
;   arc shows how far the turtle TURNS, and a blue arc shows the
;   INSIDE angle of the shape. A dotted line shows where the turtle
;   would have gone if it had not turned. A table of the numbers is
;   printed in the command center.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run, then look at the picture and the printed table.
;   Try  clearscreen angles 10 100  for a big decagon.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * the turtle's turn (outside angle) is 360 / sides
;   * turn + inside angle = 180, a straight line
;   * ARC draws part of a circle round the turtle without moving it
;   * FORM to print numbers neatly in columns
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Add up all the inside angles of a hexagon. Compare with
;     (sides - 2) x 180.
;   * What happens to the inside angle as sides gets very big?
;   * Mark only the red arcs. Do they fit together into a full circle?
; ============================================================

; A dotted line: little dashes with gaps.
to dotted :length
  repeat :length / 6 [pendown forward 3 penup forward 3]
end

; Draw a polygon and decorate each corner.
; At a corner the turtle arrives facing heading h. It is about to turn
; right by t = 360 / sides. ARC starts at the turtle's heading and
; sweeps clockwise, so:
;   the turn is the arc from h to h + t (red);
;   the inside angle is the arc from h + t to h + 180 (blue).
to angles :sides :size
  localmake "t 360 / :sides
  repeat :sides [
    setpencolor [50 50 50] setpensize 3
    pendown forward :size
    ; what the turtle would do with no turn: carry straight on
    setpensize 1 setpencolor [150 150 150]
    dotted 30 back 30
    ; red: the turn
    setpensize 2 setpencolor [220 40 40] pendown
    arc :t 22
    ; blue: the inside angle
    right :t
    setpencolor [40 90 220]
    arc 180 - :t 14
  ]
end

; Put a polygon with the given number of sides on the grid and label it.
to cell :sides :x :y
  localmake "size 380 / :sides
  penup setxy :x - :size / 2 :y setheading 90
  angles :sides :size
  penup setxy :x - 100 :y - 140 setpencolor 0
  label (sentence :sides [sides: turn] round 360 / :sides [inside] round 180 - 360 / :sides)
end

to table
  ; a word in vertical bars keeps its spaces, so the heading lines up
  print "|sides   turn   inside   inside sum|
  for [n 3 8] [
    print (sentence form :n 5 0 form 360 / :n 6 1 form 180 - 360 / :n 8 1 form 180 * (:n - 2) 12 0)
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setlabelheight 13
; heading 90 and right turns: the shapes hang down from their top side,
; so we start each one at the top
cell 3 -260 250
cell 4 0 250
cell 5 260 250
cell 6 -260 -20
cell 7 0 -20
cell 8 260 -20
table
